388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 153 0 R
/T (                    I will first give an update on the fast protein structure search tool Foldseek2, including a new 12-state alphabet complementary to 3D. Whereas the focus in developing Foldseek was on speed, the goal in developing LoL-align was to attain maximum accuracy alignments and homology detection sensitivity.  Finally, changing topics, I will describe our efforts to support computational and experimental immunologists with a toolkit for modeling peptide-MHC complexes, predicting binding to arbitrary MHC alleles, and designing peptide antigens, for instance for improved  cancer vaccines.)
/E (                    I will first give an update on the fast protein structure search tool Foldseek2, including a new 12-state alphabet complementary to 3D. Whereas the focus in developing Foldseek was on speed, the goal in developing LoL-align was to attain maximum accuracy alignments and homology detection sensitivity.  Finally, changing topics, I will describe our efforts to support computational and experimental immunologists with a toolkit for modeling peptide-MHC complexes, predicting binding to arbitrary MHC alleles, and designing peptide antigens, for instance for improved  cancer vaccines.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
