447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 157 0 R
/T (                       Protein Quantitative Trait Loci \(pQTLs\) link genetic variation and disease biology. However, standard studies lack statistical power to detect distal \(trans\)-pQTLs, and current recovery methods rely on prior knowledge. Here, we present a strategy to uncover trans-pQTLs via "co-pleiotropy": the overlap of proteins associated with variant pairs. Applying Rank-Rank Hypergeometric Overlap \(RRHO\) to the UKB-PPP and deCODE datasets, we compared variant association profiles to identify functional protein clusters without a priori assumptions. By aggregating subtle signals, we detect biologically relevant sub-threshold variants that recapitulate known protein-protein interaction networks. This framework offers a powerful tool to decode the post-transcriptional landscape of GWAS loci.)
/E (                       Protein Quantitative Trait Loci \(pQTLs\) link genetic variation and disease biology. However, standard studies lack statistical power to detect distal \(trans\)-pQTLs, and current recovery methods rely on prior knowledge. Here, we present a strategy to uncover trans-pQTLs via "co-pleiotropy": the overlap of proteins associated with variant pairs. Applying Rank-Rank Hypergeometric Overlap \(RRHO\) to the UKB-PPP and deCODE datasets, we compared variant association profiles to identify functional protein clusters without a priori assumptions. By aggregating subtle signals, we detect biologically relevant sub-threshold variants that recapitulate known protein-protein interaction networks. This framework offers a powerful tool to decode the post-transcriptional landscape of GWAS loci.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
