/T (AGAPE 2.0 - Leveraging Machine Learning and Generative Approaches to Design Selective G4 Ligands)
/E (AGAPE 2.0 - Leveraging Machine Learning and Generative Approaches to Design Selective G4 Ligands)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 162 0 R
/T (        G-quadruplexes \(G4s\) have emerged as promising therapeutic targets, yet identifying active ligands remains challenging due to the vast chemical space and costly experimental screening. We present Deep-AGAPE, an open-source machine learning framework designed to predict G4 stabilization using molecular descriptors and experimental FRET melting data. Optimized XGBoost and deep neural network models achieved F1-scores of 0.848 and 0.810, respectively. Complementing this predictive approach, G4PT integrates generative artificial intelligence to design novel potential G4 ligands, achieving 61.5% molecular validity and approximately 94% novelty. Together, these frameworks combine ligand activity prediction and molecular generation in an accessible, reproducible workflow supported by interactive web platforms to accelerate G4-targeted drug discovery.)
/E (        G-quadruplexes \(G4s\) have emerged as promising therapeutic targets, yet identifying active ligands remains challenging due to the vast chemical space and costly experimental screening. We present Deep-AGAPE, an open-source machine learning framework designed to predict G4 stabilization using molecular descriptors and experimental FRET melting data. Optimized XGBoost and deep neural network models achieved F1-scores of 0.848 and 0.810, respectively. Complementing this predictive approach, G4PT integrates generative artificial intelligence to design novel potential G4 ligands, achieving 61.5% molecular validity and approximately 94% novelty. Together, these frameworks combine ligand activity prediction and molecular generation in an accessible, reproducible workflow supported by interactive web platforms to accelerate G4-targeted drug discovery.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
