>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 163 0 R
/T (          Metastatic melanoma survival has been radically extended by immune checkpoint blockers but resistance occurs for half patients. Here, we hypothesized early on-treatment routine markers can enhance survival and response prediction together with baseline and clinical markers. We propose one model with baseline markers and also with early on-treatment routine markers on a 704 patients discovery cohort \(Cox models are fitted in survival and logistic regression in response\). We compare our models to 11 state of the art \(STOTA\) models on discovery and external validation cohorts. STOTA include baseline markers only, by adding early on-treatment markers correspondent to baseline markers, we compare gain in performances of on-treatment and baseline vs baseline markers for each models pairs. Our models beat baseline STOTA models. For each pairs, on-treatment markers improve performances and likelihood ratio test are significant.)
/E (          Metastatic melanoma survival has been radically extended by immune checkpoint blockers but resistance occurs for half patients. Here, we hypothesized early on-treatment routine markers can enhance survival and response prediction together with baseline and clinical markers. We propose one model with baseline markers and also with early on-treatment routine markers on a 704 patients discovery cohort \(Cox models are fitted in survival and logistic regression in response\). We compare our models to 11 state of the art \(STOTA\) models on discovery and external validation cohorts. STOTA include baseline markers only, by adding early on-treatment markers correspondent to baseline markers, we compare gain in performances of on-treatment and baseline vs baseline markers for each models pairs. Our models beat baseline STOTA models. For each pairs, on-treatment markers improve performances and likelihood ratio test are significant.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
