/Title (Melanoma is a malignant tumor that can metastasize and acquire resistance to anticancer treatments. Immune checkpoint blockade has significantly improved the survival of patients with metastatic melanoma. Yet half of the patients treated with this immunotherapy do not benefit from durable responses. Markers derived from RNA-sequencing are promising for potential use in clinical practice to predict response to immunotherapy. Standard approaches rely on the quantification of protein-coding transcripts, which represent a small fraction of the true diversity of RNA transcripts. This work aims explore a cohort of 163 patients to identify markers derived from the whole transcriptome, in particular, markers derived from RNAs that are little studied, referred to as the dark transcriptome. Using a k-mer based approach, we show novel markers associated with response to immunotherapy, inaccessible using standard approaches.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2533 0 R
>>
endobj
