2549 0 obj
<<
/Title (RNA structure modeling greatly benefits from the availability of structural homologs, associated with the presence of coevolving positions in multiple alignments. Direct Coupling Analysis \(DCA\) is a statistical framework leveraging significant covariations between positions. Edge-activated DCA \(eaDCA\) was recently proposed as a way to target sparser and more data-efficient models using a simple greedy algorithm for learning, typically implemented with Markov Chain Monte Carlo techniques. In this work, we revisit the learning procedure in a rigorous algorithmic setting, circumventing the #P-hardness of the computation by devising exact fixed-parameter algorithms for the treewidth parameter. We empirically observe that eaDCA models are associated with moderate treewidth values, and validate the practicality of our implementation on 41 structured non-coding RFAM families.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2536 0 R
>>
endobj
