/Title (Metastatic melanoma survival has been radically extended by immune checkpoint blockers but resistance occurs for half patients. Here, we hypothesized early on-treatment routine markers can enhance survival and response prediction together with baseline and clinical markers. We propose one model with baseline markers and also with early on-treatment routine markers on a 704 patients discovery cohort \(Cox models are fitted in survival and logistic regression in response\). We compare our models to 11 state of the art \(STOTA\) models on discovery and external validation cohorts. STOTA include baseline markers only, by adding early on-treatment markers correspondent to baseline markers, we compare gain in performances of on-treatment and baseline vs baseline markers for each models pairs. Our models beat baseline STOTA models. For each pairs, on-treatment markers improve performances and likelihood ratio test are significant.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2546 0 R
>>
endobj
2563 0 obj
<<
/Title (Structural Variants \(SV\) are genomic rearrangements affecting DNA on a large scale. By altering gene dosage, disrupting coding sequences, or creating gene fusions, SVs affect gene function. Yet their functional and evolutionary impacts remain poorly understood. Leveraging the S. cerevisiae Reference Assembly Panel \(ScRAP\) pangenome and our upgraded SV-caller MUM&Co, we comprehensively identified SVs in the species population. By integrating them into the pangenome annotation we will assess their impact on gene repertoire evolution. Combining strain-specific annotations and proteomics data will reveal the effects of SVs on protein abundance and uncover SV-derived proteins. Structural properties of newly emerged protein domains will highlight SVs contribution to protein folds evolution. Ultimately, associations between SVs and phenotypic traits will be tested to provide insight into their adaptive significance.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2548 0 R
>>
endobj
