/Title (G-quadruplexes \(G4s\) have emerged as promising therapeutic targets, yet identifying active ligands remains challenging due to the vast chemical space and costly experimental screening. We present Deep-AGAPE, an open-source machine learning framework designed to predict G4 stabilization using molecular descriptors and experimental FRET melting data. Optimized XGBoost and deep neural network models achieved F1-scores of 0.848 and 0.810, respectively. Complementing this predictive approach, G4PT integrates generative artificial intelligence to design novel potential G4 ligands, achieving 61.5% molecular validity and approximately 94% novelty. Together, these frameworks combine ligand activity prediction and molecular generation in an accessible, reproducible workflow supported by interactive web platforms to accelerate G4-targeted drug discovery.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2559 0 R
>>
endobj
