/Title (Before CRISPR became a dominant gene-editing technology, its loci were first recognized as an unusual repeat pattern in bacterial genomes. Our software, Kiwi, aims to replicate this type of discovery by leveraging pangenome graph traversal and multiple sequence alignment entropy for a homology-free search. Performance has been validated on known genome-modifying systems, CRISPR and diversity-generating retroelements \(DGR\), where it successfully detects signatures, improves recall over state-of-the-art methods, and additionally flags instances that narrowly miss classification criteria as candidates for further investigation. Furthermore, Kiwi reveals loci with unique diversification patterns in unexpected genome contexts, providing compelling motivation for a targeted exploration of these overlooked regions of the bacterial genome.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2604 0 R
>>
endobj
